  "summary": "California AG Rob Bonta issued legal guidance declaring that police sharing of ALPR data with out-of-state or federal agencies violates SB 34. EFF celebrates the bulletin as vindication of years of advocacy, including its lawsuit against the Marin County Sheriff and public-records work exposing widespread sharing.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "It is against the law for police to share data collected from license plate readers with out-of-state or federal agencies.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "The bulletin comes after EFF and the California ACLU affiliates sued the Marin County Sheriff in 2021, because his agency was violating SB 34 by sending its ALPR data to federal agencies including ICE and CBP.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "Every agency in California must follow Attorney General Bonta's guidance, review their data sharing, and cut off every out-of-state and federal agency.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
